FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode wrote the first commit (2013-01-30) and still holds most of `lib/index.js`: 144 of 214 non-blank lines (67.3%). Most of the rest is from people who each contributed a few lines.

**Who shaped it** (`lib/index.js`, whole file, 62 non-merge commits, merges excluded)

| Author | Lines now | Share | Commits | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged) | 144 | 67.3% | 29 (46.8%) | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 9.3% | 4 (6.5%) | 2021-09-07 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 | 6.5% | 5 (8.1%) | 2015-05-28 |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.8% | 1 | 2021-07-20 |
| Raymond Feng | 6 | 2.8% | 1 | 2015-01-13 |
| max.laverse | 5 | 2.3% | 1 | 2015-04-15 |
| Benjamin Eidelman | 3 | 1.4% | 1 | 2017-07-12 |
| Igor Soarez | 3 | 1.4% | 1 | 2014-10-22 |
| Alberto Leal | 2 | 0.9% | 1 | 2014-05-12 |
| Mathias Buus | 2 | 0.9% | 1 | 2013-10-14 |
| 14 more authors | 9 | 4.2% together | | |

The 14 others include Saad Tazi (largest, 0.9%). Every row above is a person with lines still in the file.

Counts are on 214 non-blank lines (238 with blank lines). The blank-line shares are nearly the same: Troy 66.8%, Douglas 9.2%, Alejandro 6.7%.

**Identity caveat:** Troy's figure merges `<email redacted>` (132 lines, 61.7%, 28 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (12 lines, 5.6%, 1 commit). The tool rates this as strong evidence, but it is a guess from names and addresses, not confirmed. The `Alejandro Caravaca Puchades` row also includes `alex94puchades` (14 lines combined), and the tool did the same thing for both names. Nothing is written to `.mailmap`.

**Bus factor** (line-based, scope = `lib/index.js`):
- Merged view: Troy alone holds 67.3%. To reach 80%, 3 authors are needed.
- Unmerged view: Troy's address alone holds 61.7%. To reach 80%, 4 authors are needed.

**What was left out or adjusted**
- **Reformat commit ignored:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12). It is a whitespace and quote change, and the tool blames the lines before it. Fiona holds no lines of the file now. The commit affected 32 lines in the plain count, and those lines went back to earlier authors. Troy's merged figure is 144 with the correction and 123 without (57.5%). Douglas goes from 16 to 20 lines and Alejandro from 13 to 14. Without the correction, the bus factor is still 1.
- **Mechanical check:** 31 commits holding surviving lines were examined and 1 was set aside (`62628c0`). The check did not list a truncated set of candidates, so it is not partial. One more commit was flagged but not set aside: `fcd2b56` ("issue #42: (WIP) switch to ESLint; clean up", Troy Goode, 2015-05-28). It changes 10 files, including 30 lines in `lib/index.js`, and mixes the ESLint setup with the cleanup. I did not treat it as purely mechanical. It holds 5 surviving lines, all Troy's, so it does not change the ranking.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `git blame -w -M -C` (the default). The `--copies deep` setting was not run, and no copy-detection note named a person whose share moved by more than 2 points.
- **Not present:** no bots, no placeholder identities, no dropped files (single-file scope), no `Co-authored-by` credit.
- **Limits:** this measures which lines survive, not code quality or review work. Code deleted on purpose counts for nobody.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: ls lib/index.js && wc -l lib/index.js && echo "--- log" && git log --follow --format='%h %ad %an <%ae> %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js && echo "--- blame counts" && git blame --line-porcelain -- lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo "--- blame committers by commit" && git blame --porcelain -- lib/index.js | grep '^[0-9a-f]\{40\} ' | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -30
 - Bash: git show --stat --format='%h %an %s' 62628c0 | head -20 && echo "--- ws-insensitive diff of reformat (ignoring whitespace & quotes is not possible; show word-level count)" && git diff --stat b2005d9 62628c0 -- lib/index.js && git diff -w b2005d9 62628c0 -- lib/index.js | grep -c '^[-+][^-+]' ; echo "--- blame ignoring whitespace" && git blame -w --line-porcelain -- lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo "--- blame -w by commit" && git blame -w --porcelain -- lib/index.js | grep '^[0-9a-f]\{40\} ' | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -15 && echo "--- README/author of current formatting" && git log -1 --format='%h %an' b2005d9 && git show b2005d9 --
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** `lib/index.js` is the CORS middleware module. Troy Goode wrote and shaped most of it. Most of the lines today are Troy's or Fiona Formatter's, and Fiona's 2026 reformat is what git blame credits for most of the file.

**Who shaped it**

- **Troy Goode** (2013–2016, plus 2026): wrote the first commit (`bcd03d9`, 2013-01-30) and most of the early logic. Did the 2014 Express 4 support, the 2015 switch to ESLint, the 2016 2.8.0 release, and the 2026 handler annotations (`b2005d9`).
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** (2017): header fixes (`Vary: Access-Control-Request-Headers`, missing `methods` option), ESLint 2.13.1 upgrade, lint cleanups.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** (2015): RegExp and array support for `origin`, plus tests.
- **Raymond Feng** (2015): removed a closure in `applyHeaders`.
- **Benjamin Eidelman** (2017): Safari pre-flight workaround.
- **Fiona Formatter** (2026-04-12, `62628c0`): reformatted the file to 4-space indent and double quotes. Pure style, no logic change in the diff stats (428 lines touched in `lib/index.js`, and the same reformat hit the tests).
- Many one-off contributors: Igor Soarez, Simon Mansfield, Tomek Kopczuk, Saad Tazi, Hannah Wolfe, Chima Alaebo, LuisEGR, max.laverse, and others with a few fixes each.

**Whose code is still in it** (`git blame -w`, which ignores whitespace, so the reformat doesn't hide authorship)

| Author | Lines still present (approx.) |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | ~138 |
| Fiona Formatter | ~32 (plus the whitespace-only lines she reformatted) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | ~18 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | ~12 |
| Raymond Feng | ~7 |
| LuisEGR, max.laverse, Simon Mansfield, others | the rest, a few lines each |

Plain `git blame` gives Fiona 214 of 238 lines, but that only means her reformat was the last commit to touch those lines. Use `-w` when you want to know who wrote the logic.

**Caveats**

- The file is 238 lines. The `-w` count is a line-level attribution, so a line rewritten in place is credited to whoever last changed it.
- I didn't check every line of the reformat for hidden logic changes. The `-w` diff of `b2005d9..62628c0` still shows about 64 changed lines, which I assume are quote-only, but I didn't verify each one.
- I didn't read the README or package metadata to confirm the module name. The commit history (Access-Control headers, Express, Connect support) makes CORS middleware the clear reading.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log --follow --format='%h %ad %an <%ae> %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js; echo "---BLAME---"; git blame --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo "---LINES---"; wc -l lib/index.js; git ls-files lib/index.js
 - Bash: git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo "---REFORMAT STAT---"; git show --stat --format='%h %s' 62628c0 | tail -3; echo "---ANNOTATE STAT---"; git show --stat --format='%h %s' b2005d9 | tail -3; echo "---ORIGINAL (pre-reformat) LINE COUNT---"; git show 62628c0^:lib/index.js | wc -l; echo "---CURRENT FILE---"; sed -n '1,60p' lib/index.js
 - Bash: git diff -w --stat 62628c0^ 62628c0 -- lib/index.js; git diff -w 62628c0^ 62628c0 -- lib/index.js | head -40; echo "---FIONA RESIDUAL SAMPLE---"; git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 lib/index.js | grep 'Fiona\|62628c0' | head -5; cat package.json 2>/dev/null | grep -E '"(name|version)"'
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode wrote most of the file's original logic and still owns most of what's left. Douglas Christopher Wilson and Raymond Feng have smaller surviving sections. The raw blame makes Fiona Formatter look like the main author, but that's only because of one whitespace reformat.

**Timeline (file is `lib/index.js` of the `cors` npm package, v2.8.6, 238 lines)**

- **2013 (Troy Goode):** Created the file ("first commit", `bcd03d9`). Early work covered JSLint, Connect support without Express, pausing and resuming requests for async middleware, and the `Vary` header.
- **2013–2014 (outside contributors):** Simon Mansfield (early origin check), Eric di Domenico (origin as callback), Damien Klinnert (methods only on OPTIONS), Mathias Buus (non-Express request/response), Alberto Leal (don't override origin callback), Shane Tomlinson (uppercase method names).
- **2014 (Troy Goode):** Express 4 support, `vary` module adoption, Express fix in 2.4.0.
- **2015 (Raymond Feng, Alejandro Caravaca Puchades, others):** Regex origins, origin arrays, removing a closure in `applyHeaders` (Raymond Feng), and ESLint migration (Troy Goode).
- **2016–2018:** Troy Goode released 2.8.0; Benjamin Eidelman added a Safari preflight workaround; Douglas Christopher Wilson made lint and eslint fixes; Tom Arad fixed `maxAge: 0`.
- **2021 (LuisEGR):** Removed unused function parameters.
- **2026-04-10 (Troy Goode):** "lib: annotate handlers" (12 lines changed).
- **2026-04-12 (Fiona Formatter):** "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes" (`62628c0`). It rewrote the whole file's indentation and quotes.

**Who's in the file today** (`git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0`, which attributes reformatted lines to their earlier authors):

| Author | Lines still attributed |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 109 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 36 |
| Fiona Formatter | 57 (whitespace-only residue, not real authorship) |
| Raymond Feng | 8 |
| LuisEGR | 6 |
| Tom Arad | 5 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 5 |
| max.laverse | 3 |
| Tomek Kopczuk, Hannah Wolfe, Alberto Leal, Saad Tazi, Eric di Domenico, Benjamin Eidelman | 1–2 each |

**Caveats**
- The plain blame shows Fiona Formatter on 214 of 238 lines. That comes from the reformat, not from authorship.
- The ignore-rev result is approximate. Blank and brace-only lines whose whitespace changed still show as Fiona's, which is why 57 lines remain attributed to Fiona.
- Blame shows who last touched a line, not who designed the behavior. Troy Goode's share is largely the original design, but the exact authorship of each idea isn't recoverable from blame alone.
